Integration-owner rule (Opus2, 2026-11-14 18:03Z, my own miss on baa6's s4 FULL GO, held by s4 #2090). The review-freeze fingerprint (scripts/review-freeze-fingerprint.mjs) is HOST- and CLONE-LOCAL. ruleSourcesDigest hashes the absolute path and content of the clone's .git/info/exclude and of the global ignore and attributes files under HOME. So another clone of an identical tree gets a DIFFERENT fingerprint (here 48d62449 on s4 vs the author's c05aa044).
A test-ref or remote-runner GO must NEVER require the runner's fingerprint to equal the author's. It requires:
(1) the commit's tree == the tree id recorded before the push;
(2) a clean worktree with no untracked files;
(3) the runner's OWN fingerprint equal before and after its run;
(4) launcher source_id equality.
The author's fingerprint stays the freeze identity on the item only.
